│  # Scan Plan                                                                 │
│                                                                              │
│  ## Objective                                                                │
│  Execute a structured market scan cycle to identify active trading           │
│  opportunities, assess prevailing market conditions, and prioritize          │
│  actionable setups for the next execution window.                            │
│                                                                              │
│  ## Cycle Parameters                                                         │
│  - **Cycle Type:** Full market scan (breadth + depth)                        │
│  - **Time Window:** Pre-session through first hour of the primary session    │
│  - **Target Universe:** High-liquidity instruments across equities,          │
│  indices, FX majors, and top-cap crypto                                      │
│  - **Data Sources:** Price action, volume, volatility metrics,               │
│  news/catalyst feed, breadth indicators                                      │
│                                                                              │
│  ## Phase 1 — Environment Assessment (Regime Check)                          │
│  1. Determine overall market regime: trending, ranging, or risk-off.         │
│  2. Review overnight/pre-session moves, gaps, and macro events on the        │
│  calendar.                                                                   │
│  3. Assess volatility regime (rising, falling, compressing) to calibrate     │
│  position sizing.                                                            │
│  4. Identify dominant themes and sectors leading or lagging.                 │
│                                                                              │
│  ## Phase 2 — Breadth Scan                                                   │
│  1. Advance/decline and new high/new low breadth.                            │
│  2. Sector rotation map — which sectors are gaining/losing relative          │
│  strength.                                                                   │
│  3. Index-level structure: support/resistance, trend alignment across        │
│  timeframes.                                                                 │
│                                                                              │
│  ## Phase 3 — Instrument-Level Scan                                          │
│  1. Filter universe by liquidity and volatility thresholds.                  │
│  2. Run momentum and mean-reversion screens against regime.                  │
│  3. Flag instruments showing breakout, retest, or exhaustion patterns.       │
│  4. Cross-check flagged names against catalyst/news flow.                    │
│                                                                              │
│  ## Phase 4 — Ranking & Prioritization                                       │
│  1. Score candidates on: trend quality, risk/reward, catalyst strength,      │
│  liquidity.                                                                  │
│  2. Rank top opportunities; discard low-conviction setups.                   │
│  3. Define triggers, invalidation levels, and position sizing for            │
│  survivors.                                                                  │
│                                                                              │
│  ## Phase 5 — Execution Prep & Handoff                                       │
│  1. Set watchlist with entry, stop, and target levels.                       │
│  2. Define max risk per position and aggregate exposure cap.                 │
│  3. Establish monitoring cadence and re-scan triggers.                       │
│                                                                              │
│  ## Deliverables                                                             │
│  - Market regime classification                                              │
│  - Ranked opportunity watchlist with levels                                  │
│  - Exposure and risk limits                                                  │
│  - Re-scan triggers and monitoring schedule                                  │
│                                                                              │
│  ## Success Criteria                                                         │
│  A prioritized, actionable watchlist aligned to the current regime, with     │
│  defined risk parameters and clear conditions under which the cycle should   │
│  be re-run.                                                                  │
