│  **Trigger:** Win/Loss Ratio from the Alpaca scan observed **2 winners / 4   │
│  losers** → Win Rate = 2/6 = **33.3%**, which is well below the 80%          │
│  threshold. Corrective action was required.                                  │
│                                                                              │
│  **Action Taken:** Activated the **Code Optimization Tool** to tighten the   │
│  EMA distance filter in `real_alpaca_backtester.py`.                         │
│                                                                              │
│  - **Parameter modified:** EMA distance multiplier                           │
│  - **Previous value:** 1.5 (default/loose)                                   │
│  - **New value:** **0.8**                                                    │
│  - **Tool confirmation:** "Successfully tightened EMA parameter to 0.8       │
│  ATR."                                                                       │
│                                                                              │
│  **Rationale:** A 33.3% win rate signals the entry logic is accepting        │
│  setups with too much distance from the EMA, allowing low-quality, extended  │
│  entries that reverse against the position. By tightening the EMA distance   │
│  from 1.5 to **0.8 ATR**, the filter now only triggers on price that is      │
│  hugging the EMA closely — i.e., only near-perfect, high-conviction          │
│  pullback/retest setups. This reduces the number of trades but raises the    │
│  average quality, targeting entries that have a much higher probability of   │
│  resolving in favor of the trend.                                            │
│                                                                              │
│  **Decision:** Tighten the EMA distance to **0.8** (aggressive tightening    │
│  rather than the intermediate 1.2) because the observed win rate (33.3%) is  │
│  far below 80% and requires a strict quality gate rather than a marginal     │
│  adjustment.                                                                 │
│                                                                              │
│  **Next Steps:** Re-run the backtester with the 0.8 ATR EMA distance filter  │
│  and re-evaluate the win/loss ratio. If win rate remains under 80%, tighten  │
│  further; if trade count collapses to near-zero while win rate rises above   │
│  80%, hold at 0.8.                                                           │
│                                                                              │
