│  Final Answer:                                                               │
│  Scan Plan                                                                   │
│                                                                              │
│  Objectives                                                                  │
│  1. Refresh market intelligence across the full target universe so the next  │
│  cycle starts from current, verified data.                                   │
│  2. Detect changes since the last cycle: new entrants, exits, pricing        │
│  moves, product launches, funding events, hiring signals, and positioning    │
│  shifts.                                                                     │
│  3. Prioritize segments by strategic relevance and volatility so limited     │
│  scanning effort lands on the highest-signal areas.                          │
│  4. Produce a clean, deduplicated, source-attributed dataset ready for       │
│  analysis and synthesis.                                                     │
│  5. Surface the top 5–10 developments that warrant immediate attention or    │
│  deeper investigation.                                                       │
│                                                                              │
│  Scope                                                                       │
│  - Segments: direct competitors, adjacent players, potential                 │
│  acquirers/partners, emerging startups, and category-defining new entrants.  │
│  - Geography: primary market plus any region flagged as strategically        │
│  important in the prior cycle.                                               │
│  - Time window: changes since the last scan date, with a 30-day lookback     │
│  for slower-moving signals (funding, hiring, patents).                       │
│  - Exclusions: noise sources with low reliability, duplicate press           │
│  releases, and purely speculative commentary without primary sourcing.       │
│                                                                              │
│  Sources and Priority                                                        │
│  - Tier 1 (primary, must-cover): company websites, pricing pages, product    │
│  changelogs, SEC/regulatory filings, official press releases, job boards,    │
│  app store updates, executive statements.                                    │
│  - Tier 2 (high-value secondary): reputable trade press, industry analyst    │
│  notes, funding databases, patent filings, conference agendas.               │
│  - Tier 3 (signal-only): social media, community forums, podcasts,           │
│  newsletters — used to generate leads, never as sole evidence.               │
│                                                                              │
│  Method                                                                      │
│  1. Re-validate the watchlist: confirm each tracked entity is still active   │
│  and relevant; add or remove based on prior-cycle findings.                  │
│  2. Crawl Tier 1 sources per entity; capture pricing, product, personnel,    │
│  and corporate changes.                                                      │
│  3. Sweep Tier 2 for funding rounds, partnerships, acquisitions, and         │
│  analyst commentary.                                                         │
│  4. Monitor Tier 3 for early signals; tag any lead for Tier 1/2              │
│  verification before inclusion.                                              │
│  5. Deduplicate and normalize: one record per event, each with entity,       │
│  date, category, source URL, and confidence level.                           │
│  6. Score each finding by impact (1–5) and urgency (1–5); rank by combined   │
│  score.                                                                      │
│  7. Flag anomalies and contradictions for manual review.                     │
│                                                                              │
│  Deliverables                                                                │
│  - Updated entity watchlist with status changes.                             │
│  - Structured findings log (entity, event type, date, source, confidence,    │
│  impact, urgency).                                                           │
│  - Top developments brief: 5–10 items with one-line significance notes.      │
│  - Open questions and gaps requiring follow-up in the next cycle.            │
│                                                                              │
│  Timeline                                                                    │
│  - Day 1: watchlist re-validation and source setup.                          │
│  - Days 2–3: Tier 1 sweep across all active entities.                        │
│  - Day 4: Tier 2 sweep and lead verification.                                │
│  - Day 5: deduplication, scoring, and ranking.                               │
│  - Day 6: top developments brief and gap analysis.                           │
│  - Day 7: review, QA, and handoff to analysis.                               │
│                                                                              │
│  Success Criteria                                                            │
│  - Every active entity has current Tier 1 coverage or a documented reason    │
│  for absence.                                                                │
│  - All findings carry a primary source or explicit confidence downgrade.     │
│  - No duplicate records in the findings log.                                 │
│  - Top developments brief delivered on schedule with actionable              │
│  significance notes.                                                         │
│  - Open questions list is specific enough to drive the next cycle's plan.    │
│                                                                              │
│  Risks and Mitigations                                                       │
│  - Source decay or paywalls: maintain two independent sources per critical   │
│  entity.                                                                     │
│  - Signal overload: cap Tier 3 intake and require Tier 1/2 confirmation.     │
│  - Coverage gaps in emerging segments: allocate a fixed discovery budget     │
│  each cycle.                                                                 │
│  - Stale watchlist: enforce re-validation at the start of every cycle.       │
│                                                                              │
│  Next Cycle Trigger                                                          │
│  Begin the next scan immediately upon delivery of the top developments       │
│  brief, or earlier if a Tier 1 source reports a material event.              │
│                                                                              │
